  "excluded": [
    "octabam's other modules, tools and gates",
    "STEM REC's working records in octabam (FLASH.md, CLEANUP.md, TODO.md)",
    "Firmware images, card data and generated packages"
  ],
  "notes": [
    "upstream/ holds STEM REC's manifest, source and README copied byte for byte from 00a23502a9e3ce8264888026a2b6764e7f52a3be; stems.s at the module root is the same file, and LICENSE is octabam's, unchanged.",
    "manifest.py is Modwerk's card-build adapter of upstream/manifest.py, changed four ways: no requires (Modwerk's builder places DramRegions at the top of its fixed reserve, where octabam's MEMORY sizes one); no YES detour at 0x4005e4c8 (APPLY SCENE patches that site and a card build has no key bus, so the main page's YES double tap is left out); the gain table as 25 stock copies of the user's OS (0x400ea18a, 774 bytes) instead of an .incbin of the OS slice; and the displaced stock instructions named by stock guards instead of written out.",
    "Card build only: a USB package would need an 8 MiB DRAM grant and a lifecycle for the module's own writer task, which the base does not offer (Discord, 5 Nov 2026)."
  ],
  "status": "Draft card-only port. Built natively and booted under ot_emu; parity, packages, qualification and hardware evidence pending.",
